# Testing Standards Cursor Rules

## Test Structure

- Write unit tests for all functions and classes
- Use pytest as the testing framework
- Organize tests in test_*.py files
- Use descriptive test function names
- Group related tests in test classes
- Use fixtures for common test setup

## Test Coverage

- Aim for at least 80% code coverage
- Test both success and error scenarios
- Test edge cases and boundary conditions
- Test all public functions and methods
- Include integration tests for API endpoints
- Test database operations with test database

## Unit Testing

- Test one function/method per test
- Use descriptive test names that explain what is being tested
- Arrange-Act-Assert pattern for test structure
- Mock external dependencies (databases, APIs, file system)
- Test both positive and negative cases
- Use parameterized tests for multiple scenarios

## API Testing

- Use FastAPI TestClient for API testing
- Test all HTTP methods (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE)
- Verify correct HTTP status codes
- Test request/response validation
- Test authentication and authorization
- Test error handling scenarios

## Mocking

- Mock external API calls
- Mock database operations in unit tests
- Use unittest.mock or pytest-mock
- Mock file system operations
- Mock time-dependent operations
- Verify mock calls when needed

## Test Data

- Use factories for creating test data
- Use fixtures for common test data
- Clean up test data after tests
- Use different test data for different scenarios
- Avoid hardcoded test values

## Database Testing

- Use test database for integration tests
- Use database transactions for test isolation
- Clean up database after each test
- Use database fixtures for common data
- Test database migrations

## Performance Testing

- Test API response times
- Test database query performance
- Use profiling tools for performance testing
- Test with realistic data volumes
- Monitor memory usage in tests

## Test Configuration

- Use separate test configuration
- Use environment variables for test settings
- Configure test database connection
- Set up test logging
- Use test-specific fixtures

## Continuous Integration

- Run tests on every commit
- Fail builds on test failures
- Generate coverage reports
- Run linting and formatting checks
- Use pre-commit hooks for testing

## Test Documentation

- Document complex test scenarios
- Explain test data setup
- Document test dependencies
- Keep test documentation updated
- Use comments for complex test logic 